# Narrow edits

Match the request to one row. Read those paths only. Do not list the repo or open other tasks.

| Request | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Review, recommendation, or a named commit | the files that commit changed |
| GlazeWM, tiling, workspaces, keybinds | `config/glazewm.yaml`, matching function in `tasks/GlazeWm.ps1` |
| Zebar bar | `config/zebar/index.html`, `config/zebar/zpack.json`, `config/zebar/volume.ps1` |
| Terminal | `config/terminal-settings.json`, `tasks/Terminal.ps1` |
| Packages | `config/packages.psd1`, `tasks/Packages.ps1` |
| Git, WSL, Node, Flow Launcher, Input Leap, appearance | that one file under `tasks/`, plus its `config/` file if the task copies one |
| Installer selection or elevation | `install.ps1` and the single task it calls |
| CI failure | the failing step in `.github/workflows/validate.yml` only |

- `git status --short` once. Keep unrelated user changes.
- Search one directory. The pattern must contain a filename, function, or version. Do not search the repo for `version`, `node`, or `Ubuntu`.
- Read at most 80 lines, and do not read a path twice. Do not read `tests/install.Tests.ps1`, `.github/workflows/validate.yml`, `README.md`, or `package-lock.json` from the start.
- After an edit, grep the changed name in `tests/install.Tests.ps1` and read the matching lines. Open a workflow file only when that grep hits it, and read only that step.
- Check syntax with the PowerShell parser on the edited script. Run one named Pester test. Do not run the full test file, `winget show`, or the installer.
- Edit `config/` in the repo. Do not touch `%USERPROFILE%\.glzr`, the registry, or running apps unless the user asked for a live change.
